{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730088-cloning-mammoths","id":730088,"title":"Cloning Mammoths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-26T15:22:53-07:00","id":730088,"title":"Cloning Mammoths","content":"Would the Mammoth Totem be transformed into a Weaver Totem if Mammoths were finally resurrected through cloning? He is a part of Griffin's brood but he is also obsessed with not fading into annihilation. If Mammoths were returned to existence, even if strictly as zoo animals, how would you rule he be transformed spiritually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:41:31-07:00","id":730181,"title":"","content":"It would be a noticeable risk of influence that would probably lead to some sabotage or appropriation after the fact to get the mammoths to survive as mammoths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:42:35-07:00","id":730194,"title":"","content":"It's... not that simple. Spiritual entities don't change on a whim, and just cloning something doesn't mean he'd instantly become &quot;Of The Weaver&quot;. He would surely take steps to protect his newborn children. This could slowly lead him away from the Red Talons and towards the Glass Walkers as the Garou who would have the best handle on the newborn mammoths. Something like this would cause quite a bit of tension, and I could actually see Pentex getting involved and offering repopulation of mammoths for &quot;a teensy weensy favour&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't see proper Weaver spirits being specially interested in mammoth spirits or the Totem. They are their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:40:42-07:00","id":730844,"title":"","content":"I would say &quot;no&quot;. If the new mammoths were strictly controlled genetically for a long period of time that they were utterly &quot;artificial&quot; life forms that could not survive on their own, then they would approach the status of domesticated animals and would eventually be rejected by Griffin. However, if they were released into the wilderness and allowed to exist as wild creatures (albeit with some human intervention in the first few decades to build up the necessary genetic diversity), then they'd just become wild creatures.<br /> <br /> Now you could get some interesting spirit conflict in the initial few decades. Mammoth could very well change in certain personality ways, but not to the point he'd become part of Weaver's brood. He might end up leaving Griffin's brood though to join Unicorn or Stag or other newly appropriate Incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:15:32-07:00","id":733332,"title":"","content":"oh if Dinosaurs were cloned, how would it affect the mokole?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:33:51-07:00","id":733371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730088-cloning-mammoths?p=733332#post733332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh if Dinosaurs were cloned, how would it affect the mokole?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only dinosaurs that we can clone right now are birds, so not very much. There's no DNA left after a minimum of 65 million years of decay. The most optimum storage possible given the time wouldn't preserve anywhere near enough DNA to accomplish this task, and there's also no present technology to make gestating and incubating the cloned dinosaurs possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:58:27-07:00","id":734604,"title":"","content":"Just because it's all about the prehistory these days and fits the topic: Frozen cave lion cubs were recently discovered. <a href=\"http://siberiantimes.com/science/others/news/n0464-meet-this-extinct-cave-lion-at-least-10000-years-old/\" target=\"_blank\">http://siberiantimes.com/science/oth...000-years-old/</a><br /> But if these were Asian Simba kin, we shall never know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":